urnout in a midterm environment, could narrow the margin but is unlikely to threaten the outcome.", "confidence": "high", "notes": ["Incumbent JB Pritzker (D) is running."]}, "overview": "Illinois Governor JB Pritzker is seeking a third term in a rematch against Darren Bailey, the downstate farmer he defeated in 2022. Recent polls show Pritzker leading by 18 to 20 points, and prediction markets give him roughly a 96 to 97 percent chance of winning. Every major race rating outfit places the contest in the Solid or Safe Democratic column.\n\nPritzker benefits from incumbency, a Democratic-leaning state, and vast personal resources, some of which he is directing toward other Democratic campaigns. Bailey has centered his challenge on cost of living and public safety, but the candidates' only debate did little to alter the race's trajectory. Barring an unexpected shift in the campaign's final stretch, Pritzker is positioned for a comfortable victory.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.98, "margin": 13.88}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.9829, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.983, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.9789, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.9753, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.9721, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.9755, "margin": 13.9}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.9748, "margin": 13.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.9823, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.9825, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.9786, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.9788, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.9803, "margin": 14.5}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.9741, "margin": 14.0}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.9899, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.9923, "margin": 15.0}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.9927, "margin": 15.0}, {"